NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: Mostly NAMING. The claim frames its novelty against "generic role-agnostic LLMLingua-style" compression, but that strawman ignores the published query-/task-/response-aware compression line (TACO-RL, LOOC, QASPC) that already conditions retention on the receiver's need — "role+task" is one such conditioning signal, not a new mechanism. The genuine mechanism delta vs RCR-Router is only granularity: span-level extraction WITHIN a message vs item-level routing of memory subsets. That is incremental, not a new axis. The packet's "NEW axis (multi-agent inter-agent comms compression — untouched)" assertion is FALSE: RCR-Router occupies exactly that axis and claims priority on it.

FATAL_COLLISIONS:
- RCR-Router (2508.04903): role+task-stage-conditioned per-agent context selection under a strict token budget to cut MAS token cost — the claim's headline novelty, explicitly claimed "first." Verified in primary abstract.
- The "generic compression is role-agnostic only" premise is refuted by TACO-RL + LOOC + QASPC (≥2 independent, verified) — receiver-need-conditioned compression is published.

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK: RCR-Router (2508.04903); Role-Aware Context Compression in Agentic AI Pipelines (2026); ACON: Optimizing Context Compression for Long-horizon LLM Agents (2025, 45 cites); TACO-RL (2024); LOOC/Response-Aware Compression (2026); QASPC; DAC (2025). Any L1 must position against RCR-Router directly and re-baseline its "generic vs role-conditioned" contrast against a QUERY/TASK-AWARE compressor (LongLLMLingua's question-aware mode or TACO-RL), not only role-agnostic LLMLingua — otherwise the comparison is again a strawman.

RATIONALE: Live ≥2-source sweep (Semantic Scholar; arXiv abstract for RCR-Router retrieved, 2508.04903) shows the narrow novelty — receiver-role-conditioned inter-agent selection at matched token budget to reduce MAS cost — is already published and self-claimed as "first" by RCR-Router (14 cites, 30% token cut at maintained quality). The residual delta is span-level vs memory-item granularity. Independently, the claim's load-bearing premise (only a role filter can drop content a generic compressor cannot) is contradicted by the verified task-/response-aware compression line. Combined with the L0's own finding that the role-conditioned advantage is CONDITIONAL and REVERSES at high verbosity, the novelty is both occupied and conditional. RED: an L1 GPU pass is not warranted on novelty grounds; if pursued, it must cite RCR-Router and use a query/task-aware (not role-agnostic) strong baseline.
